<title>NETHERLANDS: KNP BT RISES ON POSSIBLE LEYKAM SPIN-OFF.</title>
<headline>KNP BT RISES ON POSSIBLE LEYKAM SPIN-OFF.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Dutch paper and packaging group KNP BT rose 1.30 guilders or three percent to 42.90 guilders on Friday following an announcement the company was seeking a partner for its KNP Leykam paper producing unit.</p>
<p>KNP BT said the profitability in the paper industry would remain weak in the next two or three years and that it would not ignore merging its paper unit. It also said it had an ambitious growth strategy within the distribution and packaging sector.</p>
<p>Dealers the news was likely to be well received and had improved the profit prospects of the group as a whole.</p>
<p>--Amsterdam Newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
</text>
